The shop assistant checks the receipt.
She looks at me.
"What size do you need?" she asks.
"I need one size bigger, so L."
"Size M is unfortunately too tight."
"It is really much smaller than my other T-shirts."
The shop assistant smiles.
"Yes, these T-shirts are often a bit small," she says.
She takes the yellow T-shirt from the counter.
"I am going to the stockroom briefly," she explains to me.
"I will look for the right size."
"One moment, please."
"Thank you very much," I say.
The shop assistant goes into the stockroom with the small T-shirt.
I wait at customer service.
Hopefully they still have the T-shirt in size L.
